From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 18:30:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: make the eDP 1.4 LINK_RATE_SET path actually
 reachable

msm_dp_panel_read_dpcd() stores the eDP 1.4 rate-set selection, the
table index and the rate table in panel->link_info. Link training works
on link->link_params instead, which msm_dp_ctrl_on_link() fills with
only the rate and the lane count, and msm_dp_ctrl_link_train() hands
msm_dp_aux_link_configure() a local copy with the same two fields.
use_rate_set is therefore never seen where the DPCD is written,
LINK_RATE_SET is never written, and rate_set is always 0 in
msm_dp_ctrl_link_rate_down_shift().

Copy rate_set, use_rate_set and supported_rates into link_params in
msm_dp_ctrl_on_link(), and pass rate_set and use_rate_set on to
msm_dp_aux_link_configure().

Fixes: ed100aa239be ("drm/msm/dp: Enable support for eDP v1.4+ link rates table")
Link: https://github.com/FixItFoundry/zenbook-a16-linux/blob/bf8a859c6119cbc6566f8a52f17960d14bd89088/patches/rc5-20261002/0001-drm-msm-dp-make-the-eDP-1.4-LINK_RATE_SET-path-actua.patch
[Jim Martin: taken from the patch above (a cherry-pick of 582374fbcd85
 in Jesse's own tree), which has no description or Signed-off-by.
 Dropped its write of 0 to LINK_BW_SET before LINK_RATE_SET: here
 use_rate_set is only set when LINK_BW_SET already reads 0. Wrote this
 description and added the Fixes: and Link: tags.]
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
index bec30315996..1883c0d2b8a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -1665,6 +1665,8 @@ static int msm_dp_ctrl_link_train(struct msm_dp_ctrl_private *ctrl,
 
 	link_info.num_lanes = ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes;
 	link_info.rate = ctrl->link->link_params.rate;
+	link_info.rate_set = ctrl->link->link_params.rate_set;
+	link_info.use_rate_set = ctrl->link->link_params.use_rate_set;
 	link_info.capabilities = DP_LINK_CAP_ENHANCED_FRAMING;
 
 	msm_dp_aux_link_configure(ctrl->aux, &link_info);
@@ -2397,6 +2399,20 @@ int msm_dp_ctrl_on_link(struct msm_dp_ctrl *msm_dp_ctrl,
 		ctrl->link->link_params.rate = rate;
 		ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes =
 			panel->link_info.num_lanes;
+		/*
+		 * The eDP 1.4 rate-set selection is computed into
+		 * panel->link_info, but every consumer reads link->link_params
+		 * -- without this copy use_rate_set can never be seen by
+		 * msm_dp_aux_link_configure(), and rate_set is always 0 in
+		 * msm_dp_ctrl_link_rate_down_shift().
+		 */
+		ctrl->link->link_params.rate_set =
+			panel->link_info.rate_set;
+		ctrl->link->link_params.use_rate_set =
+			panel->link_info.use_rate_set;
+		memcpy(ctrl->link->link_params.supported_rates,
+		       panel->link_info.supported_rates,
+		       sizeof(ctrl->link->link_params.supported_rates));
 		if (panel->msm_dp_mode.out_fmt_is_yuv_420)
 			pixel_rate >>= 1;
 	}
-- 
